 the girls got on the on  a phone call with him  but I was at work and it's like I'll  catch him I'll catch him next time well  there there was never a next time I  actually called him  um  [Music]  on Facebook and I was at work and I  think she had shot me a message or  something and then I saw the Green Dot  by his name so I called him he had broke  his phone so it was either somebody  else's phone or he did have a computer  that he  um could video chat over Facebook with  us every once in a while so I was I  chatted with him for like 10 minutes  just kind of bsing and telling him I  miss him and I love him  when was I go shoot Riley like I have  you on the phone we should probably call  Royce and Dad so we hung up and then we  called on our family group so that they  could jump on and dad does that work  and I mean  you would never know it was gonna be  your last conversation  I should have stopped working you know  perspective what's more important  um hindsight man I should  I should have answered those calls  um they were already in Afghanistan  before we got noticed that they were  there they had already been there I  believe at least three days  uh when we found out that they were  there  yeah I was uh  just something in the back your head let  you know this is this is not going to  turn out good you're just seeing it all  unfold and what was happening and how  many afghanis were trying to get out of  out of Kabul in the in the just absolute  train wreck of you know people falling  off of the planes and trying you know  doing anything then you start to get a  grasp of how desperate the situation was  um  really leading right up to the day of  the explosion I got a call from my  friend and her husband's in the Navy  and she was like rice how are you doing  today and I was like man actually I was  like I'm having a really rough morning  and I was just complaining about stuff  and she goes okay well how's Riley like  what about Riley and I just started  crying 